  "result": "An unquoted `#` in a completion argument is now treated as an ordinary character, so completion no longer loses the rest of the line.\n\n- **Fix:** in `split_arg_string` (`src/click/shell_completion.py`), `shlex` treated `#` as a comment start by default. I turned that off with `lex.commenters = \"\"`. I also made the fish branch of `get_completion_args` fall back to an empty string if the incomplete word splits to nothing, instead of raising `IndexError`.\n- **Tests:** in `tests/test_shell_completion.py`, I added `test_split_arg_string_hash` and four `test_full_complete` cases (bash, zsh, fish, PowerShell) where `COMP_WORDS` contains `a #b`.\n- **Results:** the full suite passes (1911 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). With the source change stashed, the five new tests fail, so they do catch the bug.\n- **Changelog:** the repo uses `CHANGES.md`, not `CHANGES.rst`. I added a \"Version 8.5.1 / Unreleased\" entry. The version number is my guess, so change it if you prefer something else.\n- **Not done:** I didn't run the `examples/completion` check from the plan.\n\nI broke the test file once while editing with `sed`, then fixed it. Nothing is committed.",
